{"id": "EUVD-2026-55413", "enisaUuid": "17660e34-3df8-3bec-af11-3883236b00af", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncifs: fix cifsFileInfo leak on kmalloc failure in deferred close drain paths\n\nIn cifs_close_deferred_file(), cifs_close_all_deferred_files(), and\ncifs_close_deferred_file_under_dentry(), when a pending deferred close\nis cancelled via cancel_delayed_work(), the subsequent kmalloc_obj() to\nadd the file to the local processing list may fail under memory pressure.\nThe loop breaks immediately, but the cancelled work is no longer pending\n(it would have called _cifsFileInfo_put()), and the cfile is never added\nto file_head for processing.  The cifsFileInfo reference and the open\nserver handle both leak.\n\nFix by saving the cfile that failed allocation in a local variable,\nbreaking as before, and calling _cifsFileInfo_put() on it after\nreleasing the lock.  Any files later in the iteration are unaffected\nsince their deferred work is still pending and will fire normally.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:02:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c968b2417f6a15d35ff4b97d534af4a126cb510b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7af7ec3af091f55d01f0ebe0246d10e37f358311", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6089f561e2c31a3ba52836c75c7d2ab50d2eea41", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/32390b3f06f26e366cfb27dbac4bc0196c321535", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c2f2e83e3bbc5483730fd4ee903182761f1ae50f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cm4r-jfcj-c3ff", "CVE-2026-68312"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "088febbe-5f17-3007-ba4d-b529b05a413e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "0dcdd178-625a-3f4b-99d9-22e28697924c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "34cdfb91-f865-30ed-aa09-91392277bd4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "3b4d91ff-2769-3d08-9cc1-160d59bdbc9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "3bbe53b9-4921-3109-a31a-0a025873a779", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.6"}, {"id": "3f27aa82-6c56-38bf-9142-bd2c039bfc63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3fc065682ebbbd15b0ce0036800f4acbf765d46 <c2f2e83e3bbc5483730fd4ee903182761f1ae50f"}, {"id": "4a067d3a-3f21-3bb9-a071-a9b5f45c15cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6a78472f-d1a4-3709-9ebb-ef7f57f13df3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3fc065682ebbbd15b0ce0036800f4acbf765d46 <6089f561e2c31a3ba52836c75c7d2ab50d2eea41"}, {"id": "79e4c936-00bf-3937-8d46-5cecb64cfa67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3fc065682ebbbd15b0ce0036800f4acbf765d46 <c968b2417f6a15d35ff4b97d534af4a126cb510b"}, {"id": "8d0a86fd-51f6-3a32-97ab-61f1173f1f18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3fc065682ebbbd15b0ce0036800f4acbf765d46 <7af7ec3af091f55d01f0ebe0246d10e37f358311"}, {"id": "c9cdb28b-c627-31ba-8059-2d2b9f5f4aba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "ea71e73f-1b23-38a5-a42f-8990382a4bce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3fc065682ebbbd15b0ce0036800f4acbf765d46 <32390b3f06f26e366cfb27dbac4bc0196c321535"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4da374db-920b-395a-bbc1-903a6cf83525", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}